WEBVTT

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.434
To record reading, choose Reading as the subject, and open the learner.

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:13.435
Choose the key stage of the ARAL-Reading materials you used.

00:00:13.435 --> 00:00:16.168
Key Stage one is for Grades one to three.

00:00:16.168 --> 00:00:18.836
Key Stage two is for Grades four to six.

00:00:18.836 --> 00:00:21.703
Key Stage three is for Grades seven to ten.

00:00:22.503 --> 00:00:25.438
For Key Stage two and three, choose Basic or Plus.

00:00:25.438 --> 00:00:29.841
Then choose the week, from one to eight, and the session, from one to four.

00:00:30.641 --> 00:00:34.962
For Key Stage one, choose the guide you used, Filipino or English.

00:00:34.962 --> 00:00:40.199
Then choose, Lesson session, or, Progress Check-in, and type the session number.

00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:42.793
Mark how the session went.

00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:44.380
A star means, Did well.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.450
A triangle means, Needed help.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.107
A circle means, Not yet.

00:00:48.107 --> 00:00:50.108
This mark is your own record.

00:00:50.908 --> 00:00:52.619
You can also record a score.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:58.364
In Key Stage one, type the L A S number, the number of items, and the number of items correct.

00:00:58.364 --> 00:01:07.164
In Key Stage two, a score box appears only for sessions that have written practice, and it shows the name of the practice and the workbook page.

00:01:07.964 --> 00:01:13.285
For a Progress Check-in, type the number of items correct and the total number of items.

00:01:13.285 --> 00:01:15.099
You may also type the seconds.

00:01:15.099 --> 00:01:17.457
The report shows these check-in scores.

00:01:18.257 --> 00:01:23.913
Just like in math, you can log the whole group at once when many learners had the same session.

00:01:23.913 --> 00:01:24.508
Then save.
